\f0\b\fs48 \cf2 \expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 VHSart \'97 Horizontal Static To Blackout Cut\cf2 \strokec2 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

\fs36 \cf2 \strokec2 Implementation Prompt \'97 Native After Effects Plugin\cf2 \strokec2 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf2 \strokec2 Implement a dedicated VHSart preset named 
\f0\b \cf2 \strokec2 Horizontal Static To Blackout Cut
\f1\b0 \cf2 \strokec2 , based on the supplied reference video 
\f2 \cf2 \strokec2 video_1.mov
\f1 \cf2 \strokec2  (duration: approximately 1.045 seconds).\
The reference has two distinct temporal states:\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\ls1\ilvl0
\f0\b \cf2 \strokec2 {\listtext	1.	}Active Static State:
\f1\b0 \cf2 \strokec2  Dense, full-frame horizontal chroma/luma static with short, tightly packed horizontal segments, mixed grayscale noise, and scattered red, blue, green, purple, cyan, and other colored fragments. The noise pattern changes between frames.\
\ls1\ilvl0
\f0\b \cf2 \strokec2 {\listtext	2.	}Signal Blackout State:
\f1\b0 \cf2 \strokec2  A sudden transition to a nearly black, very dark gray frame with extremely low detail and a subtle, narrow vertical line near the extreme left edge.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \strokec2 The defining characteristic is the abrupt transition between these two states, not a gradual fade.\
\uc0\u8232 \
\uc0\u11835 \
\uc0\u8232 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf2 \strokec2 1. Inspect and Reuse Existing VHSart Engines First\cf2 \strokec2 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf2 \strokec2 Before implementing anything:\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\ls2\ilvl0\cf2 \strokec2 {\listtext	\'95	}Inspect the complete VHSart project structure and identify the existing noise, horizontal static, chroma, luma, brightness, blackout, compositing, and temporal-control implementations.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Reuse and extend existing engines wherever they already provide the required behavior.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Do not create duplicate noise, static, chroma, or blackout engines unnecessarily.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Do not modify unrelated presets or break existing functionality.\
{\listtext	\'95	}If an existing engine cannot reproduce the reference accurately, extend that engine or add the smallest necessary dedicated component.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \strokec2 The preferred architecture is a dedicated preset configuration using existing VHSart engines, with a dedicated temporal gate/controller only if the current system cannot reliably coordinate the abrupt transition.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf2 \strokec2 2. Horizontal Chroma & Luma Static\cf2 \strokec2 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf2 \strokec2 Reconstruct the first state as a dense, full-frame horizontal static field.\
Required visual characteristics:\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\ls3\ilvl0\cf2 \strokec2 {\listtext	\'95	}Coverage across 100% of the frame.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Dense, short horizontal segments and tightly packed horizontal fragments.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Mixed luma noise: black, white, gray, and intermediate values.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Scattered chromatic fragments: red, blue, green, purple, cyan, and other subtle color variations.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Fine horizontal structure rather than large square pixels or oversized blocks.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Short horizontal chroma bleeding along selected segments.\
{\listtext	\'95	}High overall density, with enough variation to avoid a uniform pattern.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Frame-to-frame changes in segment positions, lengths, brightness, and color.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \strokec2 Do not introduce:\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\ls4\ilvl0\cf2 \strokec2 {\listtext	\'95	}Large geometric distortions.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Vertical frame wrapping.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Strong RGB displacement of an underlying scene.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Large chroma smears.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Unrequested tracking bands or unrelated VHS artifacts.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \strokec2 Use the existing VHSart static/noise and chroma systems wherever possible.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf2 \strokec2 3. Abrupt Signal Cut / Blackout Controller\cf2 \strokec2 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf2 \strokec2 This is the defining behavior of the preset.\
Implement a temporal controller that switches from the active static state to a near-black signal-loss state.\
The transition must support:\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\ls5\ilvl0\cf2 \strokec2 {\listtext	\'95	}An abrupt cut.\
{\listtext	\'95	}An optional adjustable transition duration for users who want a slightly softer version.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Manual keyframe control.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Automatic procedural timing.\
{\listtext	\'95	}A frozen/static mode.\
{\listtext	\'95	}An adjustable active-static window.\
{\listtext	\'95	}An adjustable blackout start point.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \strokec2 The reference changes state at approximately the midpoint of its short duration. Treat this only as a visual calibration reference, not as a hardcoded timestamp.\
The preset must work at arbitrary composition durations and frame rates.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf2 \strokec2 Important:
\f1\b0 \cf2 \strokec2  The default reference-matching behavior should produce a sharp, immediate cut rather than a conventional slow fade.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf2 \strokec2 4. Near-Black Signal State\cf2 \strokec2 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf2 \strokec2 After the cut, produce a nearly black or extremely dark gray frame.\
Requirements:\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\ls6\ilvl0\cf2 \strokec2 {\listtext	\'95	}Darkness should cover the entire frame.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Preserve a subtle, smooth dark-gray tonal floor rather than forcing mathematically pure black in every pixel.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Keep residual texture extremely low.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Do not continue the colored static into the blackout state.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Do not introduce unnecessary scanlines, chroma noise, tracking tears, or geometric distortions.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \strokec2 The darkness level must be independently adjustable.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf2 \strokec2 5. Subtle Left Edge Line\cf2 \strokec2 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf2 \strokec2 Add an optional, independently controlled vertical line or narrow strip close to the extreme left edge.\
Characteristics:\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\ls7\ilvl0\cf2 \strokec2 {\listtext	\'95	}Very narrow width.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Very low brightness.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Slightly lighter than the surrounding dark background.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Stable and subtle.\
{\listtext	\'95	}No large glow, distortion, or noticeable displacement.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \strokec2 Provide independent controls for:\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\ls8\ilvl0\cf2 \strokec2 {\listtext	\'95	}Enable/Disable.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Width.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Horizontal position.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Brightness.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Opacity.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \strokec2 Disabling this feature must preserve its previous parameter values.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf2 \strokec2 6. Parameters and UI\cf2 \strokec2 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf2 \strokec2 Expose the following controls in the appropriate existing VHSart interface:\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf2 \strokec2 Horizontal Static
\f1\b0 \cf2 \strokec2 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\ls9\ilvl0\cf2 \strokec2 {\listtext	\'95	}Static Intensity\
{\listtext	\'95	}Horizontal Segment Length\
{\listtext	\'95	}Chroma Saturation\
{\listtext	\'95	}Luma Noise Amount\
{\listtext	\'95	}Colored Noise Amount\
{\listtext	\'95	}Static Density\
{\listtext	\'95	}Animate With Time\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf2 \strokec2 Signal Cut
\f1\b0 \cf2 \strokec2 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\ls10\ilvl0\cf2 \strokec2 {\listtext	\'95	}Blackout / Cut Amount\
{\listtext	\'95	}Blackout Start\
{\listtext	\'95	}Cut Transition\
{\listtext	\'95	}Darkness Level\
{\listtext	\'95	}Automatic / Manual Timing\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf2 \strokec2 Left Edge Line
\f1\b0 \cf2 \strokec2 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\ls11\ilvl0\cf2 \strokec2 {\listtext	\'95	}Enable Left Edge Line\
{\listtext	\'95	}Line Width\
{\listtext	\'95	}Line Position\
{\listtext	\'95	}Line Brightness\
{\listtext	\'95	}Line Opacity\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf2 \strokec2 Randomization
\f1\b0 \cf2 \strokec2 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\ls12\ilvl0\cf2 \strokec2 {\listtext	\'95	}Random Seed\
{\listtext	\'95	}Temporal Variation\
{\listtext	\'95	}Frozen Pattern\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \strokec2 Use sensible ranges and defaults based on the supplied reference. Do not expose controls that have no meaningful effect on the rendered output.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf2 \strokec2 7. Compositing and Input Modes\cf2 \strokec2 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf2 \strokec2 Support the appropriate existing VHSart compositing modes:\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\ls13\ilvl0\cf2 \strokec2 {\listtext	\'95	}Generated Static / Signal Output.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Apply Over Original.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Blend With Input.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \strokec2 The generated signal mode must be capable of producing the reference\'92s full-frame static followed by a near-black state without requiring an underlying video image.\
When blending with original footage, make the interaction between the original image, static, and blackout independently predictable. The blackout must not accidentally restore or reveal the original image unless the selected blend mode explicitly requests that behavior.\
Preserve the input alpha channel correctly. Handle premultiplied alpha consistently and avoid black or colored fringes around transparent pixels.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf2 \strokec2 8. Deterministic Temporal Rendering\cf2 \strokec2 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf2 \strokec2 Use deterministic procedural generation.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\ls14\ilvl0\cf2 \strokec2 {\listtext	\'95	}Derive the effective seed from the user seed and the composition frame/time when animation is enabled.\
{\listtext	\'95	}When animation is disabled, preserve a stable static pattern.\
{\listtext	\'95	}The same frame, parameters, and seed must produce the same output.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Rendering must remain consistent during timeline scrubbing and repeated renders.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Do not depend on previous-frame memory or render order.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \strokec2 Support After Effects multi-frame rendering and thread-safe execution.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf2 \strokec2 9. Reference Matching\cf2 \strokec2 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf2 \strokec2 Compare the actual C++ plugin output against 
\f2 \cf2 \strokec2 video_1.mov
\f1 \cf2 \strokec2  at corresponding timestamps.\
Pay particular attention to:\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\ls15\ilvl0\cf2 \strokec2 {\listtext	\'95	}Full-frame horizontal static density in the opening state.\
{\listtext	\'95	}The short, compressed horizontal segment structure.\
{\listtext	\'95	}The balance between chromatic and grayscale noise.\
{\listtext	\'95	}Frame-to-frame variation in the static pattern.\
{\listtext	\'95	}The abrupt transition around the middle of the reference.\
{\listtext	\'95	}The near-black appearance after the transition.\
{\listtext	\'95	}The extremely subtle left-edge vertical line.\
{\listtext	\'95	}The absence of unrequested geometric distortion and excessive residual noise.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \strokec2 Inspect enlarged crops as well as full-frame comparisons. Do not judge matching from a small preview alone.\
The implementation is not complete merely because the plugin compiles. It must be rendered and visually checked inside After Effects.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf2 \strokec2 10. Acceptance Criteria\cf2 \strokec2 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf2 \strokec2 The preset is complete only when:\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\ls16\ilvl0\cf2 \strokec2 {\listtext	1.	}The opening state produces dense, full-frame horizontal chroma/luma static.\
{\listtext	2.	}The static changes deterministically between frames when animation is enabled.\
{\listtext	3.	}The transition to blackout is abrupt by default.\
{\listtext	4.	}The blackout state is nearly black and substantially free of residual static.\
{\listtext	5.	}The subtle left-edge line can be independently enabled and adjusted.\
{\listtext	6.	}The preset works at arbitrary composition durations and frame rates.\
{\listtext	7.	}Alpha, premultiplication, thread safety, and multi-frame rendering are handled correctly.\
{\listtext	8.	}Existing VHSart presets and engines remain functional.\
{\listtext	9.	}The final output has been tested visually inside After Effects against the supplied reference.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf2 \strokec2 Do not create a completely new noise engine just to implement this preset. Reuse VHSart\'92s existing engines, add only the missing temporal coordination or small components, and prioritize accurate reconstruction of the two-state signal behavior.
\f1\b0 \cf2 \strokec2 \
